• You manage phone calls, emails and the agenda related to  the meetings organised by the association or to those which the executives and advisors are attending in Brussels; 

• You are in charge of making meeting preparations and execution run smoothly; 

• You are the interface for the executives, advisors and the association members as well as external interlocutors, generally high level stakeholders; 

• You are the person of confidence for anything administrative in the association’s head office, in particular you coordinate the receipt and payment of any incoming invoices and you interface with the external accountants; 

• You take the lead on certain specific department projects where appropriate and in coordination with the management; 

• You perform other management/support tasks, such as database management, and other ad hoc activities to enable the association to conduct activities on behalf of the worldwide membership. 

The ideal Executive Assistant :



• Has 3 years of experience in a similar position; 

• Speaks English, French and Dutch fluently. 

• Exhibits a passion for results; 

• Can anticipate and identify problems and solve them independently – knowing that the executives and advisors are always there with guidance; 

• Has excellent communication skills; 

• Has a “can do” attitude and thrives on making the impossible possible; 

• Is capable of establishing strong relationships both internally – including with our members – and externally with third parties; 

• Is capable of remaining calm, diplomatic and focused also when under pressure;

• Conduct in-depth analyses of P&L, ROCE, and risk management for specific market segments, identifying trends and growth potential;
• Translate financial data into clear reports and presentations, providing strategic insights and recommendations;
• Optimize working capital and monitor key risks related to accumulated positions and essential raw materials;
• Manage the planning process, including periodic forecasts, annual budgeting, and strategic planning up to EBIT level;
• Contribute to key investment projects, including CAPEX and M&A, by providing financial expertise;
• Collaborate with the Reporting Factory to enhance reporting and analysis tools, ensuring consistency and accuracy;
• Act as a strong business partner by supporting market segments and facilitating strategic decisions with financial insights.

Must-haves:

• You hold a master’s degree in finance, business administration, or a related field;
• Acquire at least 4 years of experience in finance, preferably as a controller or business partner;
• Demonstrate strong analytical skills to translate financial data into strategic insights;
• Communicate fluently in Dutch, both written and spoken;
• Possess excellent communication skills to present complex financial concepts clearly;
• Collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and senior management.
Nice-to-haves:

• Have experience working with SAP or similar ERP systems.
• Speak English or French in addition to Dutch.
• Show a proactive mindset with a hands-on approach to problem-solving.
• Bring experience in investment analysis, CAPEX, or M&A.
